// Error-rate alert condition. Deployed as the actual alert query in
// infra/modules/alerts.bicep's Microsoft.Insights/scheduledQueryRules resource
// (evaluationFrequency PT5M, windowSize PT5M, fires when this query returns any row) -
// this file and that resource's inline query must be kept identical; this copy exists so
// the query is reviewable without reading Bicep string-interpolation syntax.
//
// ${errorRateThreshold} below is the Bicep module's parameter (default 5, i.e. 5%) -
// substituted at deploy time. Shown here with the literal default for readability.
requests
| where timestamp > ago(5m)
| summarize total = count(), failed = countif(success == false)
| extend errorRatePercent = round(100.0 * failed / total, 2)
| where errorRatePercent > 5
